# Export allowlist of the plugin-shaped unload module on Mach-O (ld64
# -exported_symbols_list): its C entry points and nothing else. What a plugin
# embedding anira should do (docs/sphinx/troubleshooting.rst, "Host application
# ships its own backend runtime"), and required on macOS with a static anira and
# the ExecuTorch backend: its archives are force-loaded, and ld64 has no hidden
# variant of -force_load, so nothing short of an export list keeps executorch::/
# xnn_* out of the export table — which the anira_exports CTest asserts. Keep in
# sync with module.cpp and module.map.
_anira_test_create
_anira_test_prepare
_anira_test_process
_anira_test_destroy
_anira_test_create_throwing
_anira_test_num_inference_threads
_anira_test_has_inference_threads
_anira_test_num_sessions
_anira_test_has_core
_anira_test_shutdown
_anira_test_leak_thread
